{title: Put Out into Deep Water}
{subtitle: Luke 5:1–11}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] |
| [C] [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]We rowed out on the dark lake when the stars [C]were in the [Dm]sky
We cast and hauled the empty nets till the [C]morning sun came [Dm]high
We were washing out the [F]tackle when the [C]Teacher came a[Bb]long
He [Dm]climbed into my [F]boat and said, now [C]push us out from [Dm]shore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Put out into deep [F]water
And [C]let down your nets for a [Dm]catch
Master, we worked [F]hard all night and caught [C]nothing
But [Bb]at your word I [C]will let down the [Dm]nets
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The nets began to tear, boys, the fish [C]came leaping [Dm]in
We signaled to our partners, they came [C]rowing to the [Dm]din
We filled both boats so [F]full of fish that [C]they began to [Bb]sink
And [Dm]I fell down be[F]fore him and I [C]couldn't even [Dm]think
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Go away from me, Lord, for [F]I am a sinful [C]man
[Bb]Do not be af[F]raid
From [Bb]now on you will be catch[F]ing people [C][Gm][Bb][C][Dm][C][Bb][C][Dm][C][Bb][C]
[Dm]So they brought their [C]boats to shore, [Bb]left everything [C]be[Dm]hind
And followed [C]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]At your word I [C]will let [Dm]down the [Bb][C][Dm]nets
{end_of_verse}
